<p>Denbury posted record quarterly  results for the first quarter of 1997 with both earnings and cash flow from operations the highest ever on both a gross and per share basis.  These positive financial statistics were a result of the increased production levels and continued strong product prices. Production for the first quarter of 1997 averaged  12,256 BOE/d, an increase of 125% over first quarter 1996 levels and an increase of 21% over fourth quarter 1996 results.  Product prices remained  strong with a $20.03 average oil price per bbl for the first quarter of 1997, a 20% increase in price when compared to the first quarter of 1996.  Gas prices were also strong with an average price of $2.99 per Mcf for the first quarter of 1997, although this represented a 6% decline from the levels obtained in the first quarter of 1996.  As compared to the fourth quarter of 1996, oil prices decreased slightly (3%) and gas prices remained constant.</p>
<p>Denbury is a rapidly growing independent oil and gas company with its primary operations in the states of Louisiana and Mississippi.</p>
